WEBVTT

00:22:28.691 --> 00:22:30.115
in our prison population.

00:22:30.139 --> 00:22:31.639
(Applause)

00:22:31.663 --> 00:22:34.640
And we got carried away
with the rhetoric of punishment.

00:22:34.664 --> 00:22:36.346
And so we have "Three Strikes" laws

00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:38.347
that put people in prison forever

00:22:38.371 --> 00:22:40.917
for stealing a bicycle,
for low-level property crimes,

00:22:40.941 --> 00:22:43.409
rather than making them
give those resources back

00:22:43.433 --> 00:22:45.158
to the people who they victimized.

00:22:45.182 --> 00:22:46.581
I believe we need to do more

00:22:46.605 --> 00:22:48.609
to help people
who are victimized by crime,

00:22:48.633 --> 00:22:49.784
not do less.

00:22:49.808 --> 00:22:52.133
And I think our current
punishment philosophy

00:22:52.157 --> 00:22:53.505
does nothing for no one.

00:22:53.529 --> 00:22:56.350
And I think that's the orientation
that we have to change.

00:22:56.374 --> 00:22:57.880
(Applause)

00:22:57.904 --> 00:23:00.861
CA: Bryan, you've struck
a massive chord here.